#           A[i, j] = A[i, j] - Q[i, k] * R[k, j]
#
# This is semantically identical to the baseline code:
#   - For each (k, j), the sequence of updates to R[k, j] over i is
#     still in ascending i order; operations for different j values
#     are merely interleaved, which does not change the result of
#     floating-point additions on distinct variables.
#   - The A[i, j] updates are single assignments and are unaffected
#     by loop reordering.

